CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*cmd)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct iscsi_cmd)...)
#533: FILE: drivers/target/iscsi/iscsi_target_util.c:161:
+	cmd = kzalloc(sizeof(struct iscsi_cmd) + priv_size, gfp_mask);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

CHECK:AVOID_EXTERNS: extern prototypes should be avoided in .h files
#592: FILE: include/target/iscsi/iscsi_transport.h:100:
